FEMME does not include third-party source code. Its scripts download and run
these tools, each under its own license:

- herdr (https://herdr.dev), Apache-2.0: the terminal and agent server FEMME is built around
- Mutagen (https://mutagen.io): two-way folder sync
- Caddy (https://caddyserver.com), Apache-2.0: HTTPS for the optional public board
- ntfy (https://ntfy.sh), Apache-2.0 / GPL-2.0: phone notifications
- mise (https://mise.jdx.dev), MIT: toolchains
- claude-swap (https://github.com/realiti4/claude-swap), MIT: Claude account switching
- xterm.js (https://xtermjs.org), MIT: the board's browser terminal, loaded from a CDN

The board is built from Rust crates listed in board/Cargo.lock, under their own
licenses (mostly MIT and/or Apache-2.0).
